.temp 27

* tb_sweep_open.spice -- Stage A re-run (issue #295): open-loop output behaviour
* with BOTH inputs at the same swept common mode `dc vin` 0 -> 1.5 V and a small
* differential offset `vd` (inverting input = Vin, non-inverting = Vin + vd).
* No DC feedback: the output goes where the input stage and offset send it. The
* PWM-comparator gate approximation is on VC. DUT is the committed export.

.include '/tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/design.ngspice'
.include '/tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/opamp_two_stage.dut.spice'
.include '/tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/consumer_load.inc'

.param vd=0.001

Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Ibias vdd ibias dc 10u
Vin fbn 0 dc 0
Vinp vinp fbn dc {vd}
Xdut vdd 0 vinp fbn vc ibias opamp_two_stage
Xpwm vc pwm_in


.control
dc vin 0 1.5 0.05
option numdgt=7
wrdata /tmp/buck-stage-a-4shji_tq/sweep_open_vd1mV.dat v(vc) v(xdut.tail)
.endc
.end
